<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The Maven module of the backend (feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline, Tasks 105.100 and 120.100).

  This module has the Spring server interfaces that the plugin openapi-generator-maven-plugin makes from
  contracts/openapi.yaml, and, since the walking skeleton (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Phase 200), the product code that
  implements the two operations (the package biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.app, the main class, the controllers, the state
  checker, the error handling and the OpenTelemetry filter). Build with ./mvnw: the Maven Wrapper
  (.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties) pins the Maven version of tools/versions.env.

  The values of the build for the operation GET /info (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Task 200.120): the resource
  src/main/resources/build-info.properties is a template with the two placeholders ${build.info.version} and
  ${build.info.commit}. The execution default-resources of the core plugin maven-resources-plugin (the version is
  named here, as for each other plugin) filters the template into target/classes/build-info.properties. The property
  build.info.version is the constant of the pom (0.1.0, the version of the contract, and not a value of git). The
  property build.info.commit has the default unknown in the pom, and each just recipe that starts Maven replaces it
  with the value of git rev-parse HEAD of the work tree (the function backend_maven_args of tools/gates/_lib.sh).
  The unit tests load the values of the build from a resource of the test classpath (a configurable resource name of
  the class BuildInfoProvider), so the test changes the value of the build and sees the change of the response (ACC-003).

  The plugin has two executions (see the <build> section):
    - spring-interfaces, bound to the phase generate-sources. It writes the Java code to src/generated/java, and
      adds this folder as a compile source root (the plugin option addCompileSourceRoot, so no other plugin).
      `just generate` deletes the folder first and makes the code again. The folder is committed to git.
    - api-docs, bound to no phase (the HTML documentation, REQ-015). `just api-docs` starts it. It writes to
      build/api-docs (the folder is not in git).
  `just generate`, `just compile` and `just api-docs` compare the sha256 of the plugin jar with the pin
  OPENAPI_GENERATOR_MAVEN_PLUGIN_SHA256 of tools/versions.env before they start Maven (tools/gates/_lib.sh,
  verify_generator_plugin). The version of the plugin in this file and the version in tools/versions.env must
  be the same: `just check-pins` checks it.

   The libraries (the license of each one is in the plan of feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline):
      - NO bill of materials (BOM) is imported. A BOM can bring jakarta.annotation-api in again (EPL-2.0 OR GPL-2.0
        with Classpath-exception), and the owner decided on 2026-11-04 to use org.apache.tomcat:tomcat-annotations-api
        for jakarta.annotation.Generated. The Spring Boot BOM manages that artifact too (11.0.27), so the version of
        the artifact is named here (11.0.29, the Jakarta Annotations 3.0 of the Tomcat 11.0.x line). The scope of the artifact is provided (the annotation has SOURCE
        retention), so it stays off the runtime class path. `./mvnw dependency:tree` must not show jakarta.annotation-api.
      - The generator options annotationLibrary=none, documentationProvider=none and openApiNullable=false remove
        swagger-annotations-jakarta and jackson-databind-nullable. The generated code does not need them.

    The libraries of the walking skeleton (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Phase 200; the license of each one is in the
    license table of the plan):
      - Spring Boot (org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-web, the 4.0.x line, the version 4.0.9 with the
        Spring Framework 7.0.10; the rework of 2026-11-17, because the Spring Framework 6.2.19 of the Spring Boot
        3.5.x line has two findings that are Critical without a fix): the web service (the embedded Tomcat 11, the
        Jackson 3 (the packages tools.jackson) of spring-boot-starter-jackson, spring-webmvc). NO BOM is imported, as
        above: the version is named here. Two exclusions of the starter (the owner's decisions, the plan records them):
        * spring-boot-starter-logging is excluded: it brings logback (EPL-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1, and the single-license
          form of the SBOM is not in the permitted list), and the logging implementation is spring-boot-starter-log4j2
          (the artifacts log4j-slf4j2-impl, log4j-core, log4j-jul and log4j-api, each Apache-2.0, the version
          2.25.5 that the declaration direct names - the version without the finding of the OSV data, REQ-008).
        The embedded Tomcat: the starter brings it at the version 11.0.27, and the declaration direct names the
        version 11.0.29 (the last version of the 11.0.x line, with no finding in the OSV data, REQ-008).
        * jakarta.annotation:jakarta.annotation-api is excluded: the owner decided on 2026-11-04 (the finding F1 of
          feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline) that the module must not have this artifact (EPL-2.0 OR GPL-2.0 with
          Classpath-exception); the annotation jakarta.annotation.Generated comes from org.apache.tomcat:
          tomcat-annotations-api above. The exclusions of the starter log4j2 are the same two.
      - The slf4j API (org.slf4j:slf4j-api, the 2.x line, the version 2.0.20 that Spring Boot 4.0.9
        manages): the declaration is direct (and not transitive), because the test tool testcontainers has the
        slf4j-api 1.7.36 as its dependency (the depth 2), and the bridge has it as the depth 3 (the starter, the
        bridge, the API). The resolution of Maven gives the nearest dependency (the 1.7.36), and the bridge of the
        2.x line finds no provider. The MIT of the API is in the permitted list.
        `./mvnw dependency:tree` must not show jakarta.annotation-api, and the SBOM must not have logback.
      - OpenTelemetry (io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-sdk and io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-exporter-otlp, the
        version 1.68.0, each Apache-2.0, the dependencies are Apache-2.0 too, the plan records the rows): the SDK of
        the signal trace (the one server span per request in the filter of the package app, DEC e3eadec0-a6ea-4efe-
        8e6d-fd19287122fa), and the exporter OTLP/HTTP (the artifact opentelemetry-exporter-otlp is the HTTP
        exporter of the 1.x line, the sender okhttp, and not the gRPC tree). The exporter is built in the
        configuration of the application only if the endpoint of the environment variable OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
        (or OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT) is set; with no endpoint the SDK runs with no processor, and the
        trace identifier of each request is still real (the app starts and serves, and the feature gives no collector).

   The test tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 110, Tasks 110.100 and 110.130). The module has no
   product code, so the tests exercise the generated code (the example module). The license of each tool is in the
   license table of the plan; the two tools of the class Review (JUnit and jqwik, both EPL-2.0) have the deviation
   DEC 93a6d588-e002-4daf-9a47-45e2d77786e9 (the register of the approved deviations, accepted 2026-11-09). Every
   test tool is in <scope>test</scope>, so the cyclonedx plugin (includeTestScope, the default false) keeps them out
   of the SBOM: the licenses that the SBOM gate checks are the ones of the main dependencies above.
     - JUnit (org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter): the unit tests. The version is the one of tools/versions.env
       (JUNIT_VERSION). The 5.x line and not the 6.x line: jqwik 1.10.2 needs the JUnit Platform 1.14.x, and the
       engines of the two lines do not mix (the plan records the decision).
     - Testcontainers (org.testcontainers:testcontainers and the module org.testcontainers:postgresql,
       org.testcontainers:junit-jupiter): the integration tests (one lightweight container, postgres:16-alpine, the
       PostgreSQL license; the driver org.postgresql:postgresql is BSD-2-Clause). The version is the one of
       tools/versions.env (TESTCONTAINERS_VERSION, POSTGRESQL_VERSION). The 1.21.x line and not the 2.x core: the
       junit-jupiter module has no 2.x release, and the core and the modules must be the same line (the plan records
       the decision).
     - jqwik (net.jqwik:jqwik, EPL-2.0, the deviation DEC above): the property tests. The version is the one of
       tools/versions.env (JQWIK_VERSION).
      - maven-surefire-plugin (the version in tools/versions.env, MAVEN_SUREFIRE_PLUGIN_VERSION): runs the tests of
        the JUnit Platform (the JUnit engine and the jqwik engine).
      - PIT (org.pitest:pitest-maven, the build plugin, and org.pitest:pitest-junit5-plugin, the JUnit5 support of
        PIT as a dependency of the plugin): the mutation tests (the recipe mutation-backend). The versions are the
        ones of tools/versions.env (PIT_VERSION, PIT_JUNIT5_PLUGIN_VERSION). The configuration restricts the run to
        the generated model code (targetClasses) and to the unit tests of the generated code (targetTests, the class
        that is not successful and the integration test are no target tests), and it makes the HTML and the XML
        report in target/pit-reports (the folder is in .gitignore through target/). The plugin has no execution
        bound to a phase: the recipe starts the goal mutationCoverage after the phase test-compile in one run of
        ./mvnw (the generator execution of the phase generate-sources adds src/generated/java as a compile source
        root; without the phase, the project has no compile source root, and the goal skips).
       - JaCoCo (org.jacoco:jacoco-maven-plugin, the build plugin, EPL-2.0, the deviation DEC above): the coverage
        of the module (the recipe coverage-backend). The version is the one of tools/versions.env (JACOCO_VERSION).
        The plugin has no execution bound to a phase: the recipe starts the goals prepare-agent, the phase test
        (the unit tests, the normal run of surefire) and report in one run of ./mvnw, as for the mutation tool
        pitest-maven. prepare-agent sets the project property argLine, and the test runner maven-surefire-plugin
        (that has no own argLine) passes it to the forked JVM. The report (HTML and XML) is in target/site/jacoco
        (the folder is in .gitignore through target/). The configuration has no check goal and no rule: the recipe
        makes a report and no threshold is set (REQ-006, the walking skeleton sets the threshold from the
        measured baseline).

    The architecture tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 130, Tasks 130.100 and 130.120; DEC
    9edc1071-4fd0-48b6-a037-1a4cb2331f73). Every one is in <scope>test</scope>, so the cyclonedx plugin keeps it
    out of the SBOM, as for the test tools above. The versions are the ones of tools/versions.env (SPRING_MODULITH_VERSION,
    ARCHUNIT_VERSION and STRUCTURIZR_VERSION; just check-pins compares them, check_pins.py: check_maven_test_pins).
      - Spring Modulith (org.springframework.modulith:spring-modulith-core): the module structure of the module
        (R1, the recipe architecture-backend). The 2.0.x line (2.0.9), the line of Spring Boot 4.0.x (the rework of
        feat-9-walking-skeleton, 2026-11-17; the module had the 1.4.x line with the Spring Framework 6.2.19 before).
        The core of 2.0.9 has the dependencies spring-core and spring-context 7.0.9 (the module has 7.0.10, the
        nearest dependency wins), and it gives the module structure assertions (ApplicationModules.of(...),
        verify(), detectViolations()); the JUnit test starts them without a Spring context. The test support
        artifact (spring-modulith-test) is not in the module: its annotation @ApplicationModuleTest boots a Spring
        context (the annotation is wired to @SpringBootTest), and the test of the module structure needs none.
       - Spring Boot (org.springframework.boot:spring-boot): the jar is in the module in the scope compile through the
         starter spring-boot-starter-web (the service ships it, so the jar is in the SBOM, and the test classpath has
         it too). In the line 1.4.x of Spring Modulith the module detection (ApplicationModules.of(...)) called the
         class ConfigDataEnvironmentPostProcessor of this jar, and a start without the jar stopped with the error
         NoClassDefFoundError; that was the reason of the test dependency of feat-7-verification-architecture-tools.
         The pom has no declaration of this jar (a declaration direct in the scope test would win the resolution of
         the scope over the dependency of the starter, and the main code would not compile).
      - ArchUnit (com.tngtech.archunit:archunit and archunit-junit5): the layer rule of the module (R2, the recipe
        architecture-backend), and the source of the package dependencies of the comparison with the model (the
        recipe architecture-model). The core of Spring Modulith has the dependency archunit 1.4.2; the module names
        1.5.1, and the resolution of Maven gives 1.5.1 (the nearest dependency wins).
       - structurizr-client (com.structurizr:structurizr-client): the reader of the workspace of model/
         (com.structurizr.io.json.JsonReader, the model classes of structurizr-core). The module has no other reader
         of the workspace, so the client artifact (the JSON reader) and not the DSL artifact
         (structurizr-dsl, that has the client as a dependency and the parsers for the other formats) is in the
         module. The dependencies of the client (jackson-databind, httpclient5, jaxb-api and structurizr-core) are
         in the scope test too, and the cyclonedx plugin keeps them out of the SBOM.

    The product code of the walking skeleton is in src/main/java/biz/dfch/specmgrdemo/app/ (feat-9-walking-skeleton,
    Phase 200): the main class, the two controllers, the check of the state, the handler of the error, the filter
    and the configuration of OpenTelemetry (the header comment above gives the libraries). The test classes are in
    src/test/java/biz/dfch/specmgrdemo/app/ (the unit tests and the integration tests of the walking skeleton), in
    src/test/java/biz/dfch/specmgrdemo/testtools/ (the test tools of the phases 110 and 120) and in
    src/test/java/biz/dfch/specmgrdemo/architecture/ (the architecture tools of the phase 130: the module structure
    R1, the layer rule R2 and the comparison with the model of the recipe architecture-model). The test resources
    are in src/test/resources/ (the two files build-info-test.properties and build-info-test-changed.properties,
    the seam of the unit test of the value of the build). A class whose name has no suffix `Test` (or `IT` for the
    integration tests) is a case that is not successful (ACC-002 of the plan): the default run of surefire does not
    start it, and the recipes run it separately and stop for it (tools/gates/test-*-*.sh and
    tools/gates/architecture-*.sh). The suffix IT keeps the integration tests out of the unit run.
 -->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <groupId>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo</groupId>
  <artifactId>backend</artifactId>
  <version>0.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <name>biz.dfch.SpecMgrDemo backend</name>
  <description>The Java backend: the generated Spring server interfaces and, since the walking skeleton (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Phase 200), the product code that implements the two operations (the package biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.app).</description>

  <licenses>
    <license>
      <name>GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only</name>
      <url>https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt</url>
    </license>
  </licenses>

  <properties>
    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
    <!-- The JDK of tools/versions.env (JDK_VERSION) is Temurin 21. -->
    <maven.compiler.release>21</maven.compiler.release>
    <!-- A fixed time stamp, so that the archives of a build are the same in each run. -->
    <project.build.outputTimestamp>2026-11-04T00:00:00Z</project.build.outputTimestamp>

    <!-- The generator. tools/versions.env has the same version (OPENAPI_GENERATOR_MAVEN_PLUGIN_VERSION). -->
    <openapi-generator.version>7.27.0</openapi-generator.version>
    <!-- The libraries that the generated code needs. Each version is named here, and no BOM gives one. -->
    <spring.version>7.0.10</spring.version>
    <jakarta-validation.version>3.1.1</jakarta-validation.version>
    <jackson-annotations.version>2.21</jackson-annotations.version>
    <tomcat-annotations-api.version>11.0.29</tomcat-annotations-api.version>
    <!-- The libraries of the walking skeleton (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Phase 200). Each version is named here,
         and no BOM gives one (the header comment gives the exclusions of the starters). Spring Boot is the 4.0.x
         line, the version 4.0.9 (the rework of 2026-11-17: the line 3.5.x has the Spring Framework 6.2.19, and
         the artifact spring-webmvc 6.2.19 has two findings that are Critical without a fix in the 6.2.x line; the
         Spring Boot 4.0.9 has the Spring Framework 7.0.10, the version without a finding of the OSV data). The
         version is the same as the pin SPRING_BOOT_VERSION of tools/versions.env, and the Spring Framework
         version of the property spring.version (7.0.10) is the one that the starter names. -->
    <spring-boot.version>4.0.9</spring-boot.version>
    <!-- The embedded Tomcat (the artifacts of the starter-tomcat-runtime that the starter web brings in, at the
         version 11.0.27 of the starter). The declaration direct (the depth 1) gives the version 11.0.29, the last
         version of the 11.0.x line on Maven Central (checked on 2026-11-17, the OSV data has no finding for it,
         REQ-008). -->
    <tomcat-embed.version>11.0.29</tomcat-embed.version>
    <!-- The log4j2 (the artifacts of the starter log4j2 that the starter brings in, at the version 2.24.3).
         The declaration direct gives the version 2.25.5: the OSV data has findings (Medium) for the 2.24.3,
         and the version 2.25.5 is the version without them (the same reasoning, REQ-008). The four
         artifacts must be the same version (the line of log4j2). -->
    <log4j2.version>2.25.5</log4j2.version>
    <opentelemetry.version>1.68.0</opentelemetry.version>
    <!-- The core plugin maven-resources-plugin (the version that the pinned Maven 3.10.0 binds, see the license
         table of the plan): it filters the template src/main/resources/build-info.properties (the header comment). -->
    <maven-resources-plugin.version>3.5.0</maven-resources-plugin.version>
    <!-- The values of the build for the operation GET /info (Task 200.120, the header comment). The version is the
         constant of the project (0.1.0, the version of the contract), and not a value of git. The commit has the
         default unknown, and each just recipe that starts Maven replaces it with git rev-parse HEAD. -->
    <build.info.version>0.1.0</build.info.version>
    <build.info.commit>unknown</build.info.commit>
    <!-- The test tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 110). Each version is the one of
         tools/versions.env (just check-pins compares them). The scope of every test tool is test. -->
    <junit.version>5.14.4</junit.version>
    <testcontainers.version>1.21.4</testcontainers.version>
    <postgresql.version>42.7.14</postgresql.version>
    <jqwik.version>1.10.2</jqwik.version>
    <maven-surefire-plugin.version>3.6.1</maven-surefire-plugin.version>
    <!-- The mutation tests (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 120). Each version is the one of
         tools/versions.env (just check-pins compares them). -->
    <pitest.version>1.30.2</pitest.version>
    <pitest-junit5-plugin.version>1.2.3</pitest-junit5-plugin.version>
    <!-- The architecture tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 130). Each version is the one of
          tools/versions.env (just check-pins compares them). The scope of every architecture tool is test.
          Spring Modulith is the 2.0.x line (2.0.9, the line of Spring Boot 4.0.x; see the header comment). -->
    <spring-modulith.version>2.0.9</spring-modulith.version>
    <archunit.version>1.5.1</archunit.version>
    <structurizr.version>6.2.4</structurizr.version>
    <!-- The coverage (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 140). The version is the one of
         tools/versions.env (just check-pins compares it, check_pins.py: check_maven_test_pins). -->
    <jacoco.version>0.8.16</jacoco.version>

    <!-- The files that the generators read and write, relative to the folder of this module. -->
    <contract.file>${project.basedir}/../contracts/openapi.yaml</contract.file>
    <generated.java.dir>${project.basedir}/src/generated</generated.java.dir>
    <api-docs.dir>${project.basedir}/../build/api-docs</api-docs.dir>
  </properties>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- ResponseEntity and the annotations of Spring Web MVC (@RequestMapping, @RequestParam and others). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-web</artifactId>
      <version>${spring.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- @Validated of the generated interfaces. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-context</artifactId>
      <version>${spring.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Jakarta Bean Validation, the API only (no implementation: the generated code needs none to compile). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>jakarta.validation</groupId>
      <artifactId>jakarta.validation-api</artifactId>
      <version>${jakarta-validation.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- @JsonProperty and @JsonValue of the generated model classes. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.fasterxml.jackson.core</groupId>
      <artifactId>jackson-annotations</artifactId>
      <version>${jackson-annotations.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- jakarta.annotation.Generated (Jakarta Annotations 2.1) in place of jakarta.annotation-api. Decision of the
          owner of 2026-11-04. The version is named here, and no BOM gives it. The scope is provided: the annotation
          has SOURCE retention (it is read at compile time only), so the jar stays off the runtime class path, and a
          later Spring Boot starter cannot bring jakarta.annotation-api in again with a duplicate class. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.tomcat</groupId>
      <artifactId>tomcat-annotations-api</artifactId>
      <version>${tomcat-annotations-api.version}</version>
      <scope>provided</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The web service of the walking skeleton (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Task 200.110, the header comment gives
         the exclusions): the embedded Tomcat, the Jackson and spring-webmvc. The version is named, no BOM. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
      <version>${spring-boot.version}</version>
      <exclusions>
        <!-- The logging starter brings logback (EPL-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1): not in the permitted list. The
             implementation is the starter log4j2 below (the owner's decision, the plan records it). -->
        <exclusion>
          <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
          <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-logging</artifactId>
        </exclusion>
        <!-- The finding F1 of feat-6 (the owner, 2026-11-04): the module must not have jakarta.annotation-api. -->
        <exclusion>
          <groupId>jakarta.annotation</groupId>
          <artifactId>jakarta.annotation-api</artifactId>
        </exclusion>
      </exclusions>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The logging implementation in place of logback (the header comment): the artifacts log4j-slf4j2-impl,
         log4j-core, log4j-jul and log4j-api, each Apache-2.0. The exclusions are the two of the starter web. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-log4j2</artifactId>
      <version>${spring-boot.version}</version>
      <exclusions>
        <exclusion>
          <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
          <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-logging</artifactId>
        </exclusion>
        <exclusion>
          <groupId>jakarta.annotation</groupId>
          <artifactId>jakarta.annotation-api</artifactId>
        </exclusion>
      </exclusions>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The slf4j API (the header comment): the bridge log4j-slf4j2-impl of the starter log4j2 needs the 2.x
         line of the API. Without the declaration direct, the resolution of Maven gives the 1.7.36 of the test
         tool testcontainers (the nearest dependency wins, the depth 2 against the depth 3), and the bridge
         finds no provider of the 2.x line. The version is the one that the bridge names (the POM of
         Spring Boot 4.0.9 manages 2.0.20, and the bridge log4j-slf4j2-impl 2.25.5 needs the 2.x line). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>
      <artifactId>slf4j-api</artifactId>
      <version>2.0.20</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The embedded Tomcat at the version without the finding of the OSV data (the property and the comment
         above, REQ-008): the three artifacts of the starter-tomcat, the version direct. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.tomcat.embed</groupId>
      <artifactId>tomcat-embed-core</artifactId>
      <version>${tomcat-embed.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.tomcat.embed</groupId>
      <artifactId>tomcat-embed-el</artifactId>
      <version>${tomcat-embed.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.tomcat.embed</groupId>
      <artifactId>tomcat-embed-websocket</artifactId>
      <version>${tomcat-embed.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The log4j2 at the version without the finding of the OSV data (the property and the comment above,
         REQ-008): the four artifacts of the starter log4j2, the version direct, the same version for each. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.logging.log4j</groupId>
      <artifactId>log4j-api</artifactId>
      <version>${log4j2.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.logging.log4j</groupId>
      <artifactId>log4j-core</artifactId>
      <version>${log4j2.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.logging.log4j</groupId>
      <artifactId>log4j-jul</artifactId>
      <version>${log4j2.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.logging.log4j</groupId>
      <artifactId>log4j-slf4j2-impl</artifactId>
      <version>${log4j2.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- OpenTelemetry (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Task 200.110, DEC e3eadec0-a6ea-4efe-8e6d-fd19287122fa): the SDK
         of the signal trace (the one server span per request, the header comment). Each artifact is Apache-2.0. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>io.opentelemetry</groupId>
      <artifactId>opentelemetry-sdk</artifactId>
      <version>${opentelemetry.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The exporter OTLP/HTTP (the artifact is the HTTP exporter of the 1.x line, the sender okhttp, and not the
         gRPC tree; the header comment gives the behavior with and without the endpoint of the environment). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>io.opentelemetry</groupId>
      <artifactId>opentelemetry-exporter-otlp</artifactId>
      <version>${opentelemetry.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The test tools (the scope test keeps them out of the SBOM, see the header comment). -->
    <!-- JUnit 5 (EPL-2.0, the deviation DEC 93a6d588-e002-4daf-9a47-45e2d77786e9). The 5.x line: jqwik needs the
         JUnit Platform 1.14.x. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
      <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
      <version>${junit.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Testcontainers (MIT): the core, the JUnit module and the PostgreSQL module, the 1.21.x line (see the header). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
      <artifactId>testcontainers</artifactId>
      <version>${testcontainers.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
      <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
      <version>${testcontainers.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
      <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
      <version>${testcontainers.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The JDBC driver of the container (BSD-2-Clause, test scope only: not in the SBOM). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
      <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
      <version>${postgresql.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- jqwik (EPL-2.0, the deviation DEC 93a6d588-e002-4daf-9a47-45e2d77786e9): the property tests. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>net.jqwik</groupId>
      <artifactId>jqwik</artifactId>
      <version>${jqwik.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The architecture tools (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 130; see the header comment). The
         scope test keeps them out of the SBOM. -->
    <!-- Spring Modulith (Apache-2.0): the module structure (R1). The 2.0.x line (2.0.9, the line of Spring Boot
         4.0.x: the core has the dependencies spring-core and spring-context 7.0.9, and the module has the
         Spring Framework 7.0.10 line; the plan records the decision). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.modulith</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-modulith-core</artifactId>
      <version>${spring-modulith.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The jar org.springframework.boot:spring-boot is in the module in the scope compile through the starter
         spring-boot-starter-web (the version spring-boot.version). There is no declaration of the scope test: a
         declaration direct of the scope test would win the resolution of the scope over the dependency of the
         starter (the nearest dependency wins), and the main code would not compile (the class SpringApplication
         of the jar). The jar is in the SBOM (the service ships it), and it is on the test classpath. -->
    <!-- ArchUnit (Apache-2.0, the bundled OW2 ASM is BSD-3-Clause): the layer rule (R2) and the package
         dependencies of the comparison with the model. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.tngtech.archunit</groupId>
      <artifactId>archunit</artifactId>
      <version>${archunit.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.tngtech.archunit</groupId>
      <artifactId>archunit-junit5</artifactId>
      <version>${archunit.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- structurizr-client (Apache-2.0): the reader of the workspace of model/ (the JSON reader and the model
          classes). The comparison test of the recipe architecture-model (Task 130.120). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.structurizr</groupId>
      <artifactId>structurizr-client</artifactId>
      <version>${structurizr.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- The test tools of the walking skeleton (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Phase 200; the scope test keeps them out
          of the SBOM, as for the tools above). -->
    <!-- spring-test (Apache-2.0): the MockMvc and the mock objects of the unit tests (the standalone setup, and not
          a context of Spring Boot). The version is the one of the module (spring.version, the same as the starters).
          The extension SpringExtension of the artifact is not used: it needs JUnit Jupiter 6 (the method
          computeIfAbsent of the store), and the module has JUnit Jupiter 5.14.4 (the integration tests start the
          service with SpringApplication, the class RunningService of the tests, and not with @SpringBootTest). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-test</artifactId>
      <version>${spring.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- json-path (Apache-2.0): the assertions on the JSON of the responses of the unit tests (the library of the
          method jsonPath of MockMvc, that the artifact spring-test references at run time). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.jayway.jsonpath</groupId>
      <artifactId>json-path</artifactId>
      <version>2.10.0</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
    <!-- opentelemetry-sdk-testing (Apache-2.0): the in-memory exporter of the unit test of the filter (one server
          span per request, the kind SERVER and the name of the operation). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>io.opentelemetry</groupId>
      <artifactId>opentelemetry-sdk-testing</artifactId>
      <version>${opentelemetry.version}</version>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- The resources of the module (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Task 200.120): the list of the model (and not a
         configuration of the plugin, that the parameter resources of the mojo resources of
         maven-resources-plugin 3.5.0 reads as read-only), with the filtering of the execution default-resources
         on: the file src/main/resources/build-info.properties is filtered into target/classes/build-info.properties
         with the two properties build.info.version and build.info.commit (the header comment). A value of the
         property that the build does not replace stays the default of the pom (the version 0.1.0, the commit
         unknown). The list of the test resources (the default src/test/resources) is not changed. -->
    <resources>
      <resource>
        <directory>src/main/resources</directory>
        <filtering>true</filtering>
      </resource>
    </resources>
    <plugins>
      <!-- The core plugin for the resources (feat-9-walking-skeleton, Task 200.120). The version is the one that
           the pinned Maven 3.10.0 binds (the license table of the plan); the configuration is the list of the
           resources of the model above (the parameter is read-only in the version 3.5.0). -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-resources-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${maven-resources-plugin.version}</version>
      </plugin>
      <!-- The test runner (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 110). The version is the one of
           tools/versions.env (MAVEN_SUREFIRE_PLUGIN_VERSION). The default includes of surefire (Test*, *Test,
           *Tests, *TestCase) keep the cases that are not successful (the classes without a suffix, see the header)
           out of the unit run. The tests of the JUnit Platform (the JUnit engine and the jqwik engine) are found
           without further configuration. -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${maven-surefire-plugin.version}</version>
      </plugin>
       <!-- The mutation tests (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 120, Task 120.100). No execution is
            bound to a phase: the recipe mutation-backend starts the goal after the phase test-compile in one run
            of ./mvnw (./mvnw test-compile org.pitest:pitest-maven:<PIT_VERSION>:mutationCoverage
            -Dcodegen.skip=true). The phase is necessary: the generator execution of the phase generate-sources
            adds src/generated/java as a compile source root, and the goal skips a project with no compile source
            root. PIT mutates the compiled classes of the module (target/classes, the generated code; the module
            has no product code) and runs the target tests on each mutant.
           The configuration keeps the run small and deterministic (the plan records it, Result of the Phase 120):
           - targetClasses: the generated model code only. The package biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.api has the interface
             StatusApi, and an interface has no bytecode with logic, so there is no mutant in it.
           - targetTests: the unit tests of the generated code only. The class that is not successful (no suffix
             Test) and the integration test (the suffix IT, it needs the Docker daemon) are no target tests.
            - outputFormats: the HTML report (the default folder target/pit-reports) and the XML report
              (mutations.xml, the deterministic source the recipe asserts on for the surviving mutants).
           The JUnit5 support of PIT (the JUnit engine of the JUnit Platform and the jqwik engine) is the plugin
           dependency pitest-junit5-plugin: pitest-maven loads the test framework plugins from its own classpath,
           and not from the test classpath of the module. -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
        <artifactId>pitest-maven</artifactId>
        <version>${pitest.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <targetClasses>
            <param>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.model.*</param>
          </targetClasses>
          <targetTests>
            <param>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.testtools.ErrorCodeTest</param>
            <param>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.testtools.ErrorCodePropertyTest</param>
          </targetTests>
          <outputFormats>
            <outputFormat>HTML</outputFormat>
            <outputFormat>XML</outputFormat>
          </outputFormats>
        </configuration>
        <dependencies>
          <dependency>
            <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
            <artifactId>pitest-junit5-plugin</artifactId>
            <version>${pitest-junit5-plugin.version}</version>
          </dependency>
        </dependencies>
      </plugin>
       <!-- The coverage (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 140, Task 140.110). No execution is
            bound to a phase: the recipe coverage-backend starts the goals prepare-agent, the phase test and
            report in one run of ./mvnw (the same way as pitest-maven, see above). The goal prepare-agent sets
            the project property argLine before the phase test runs, and the test runner
            maven-surefire-plugin (that has no own argLine configuration) passes it to the forked JVM. The
            goal report reads the execution data (target/jacoco.exec) and makes the report in
            target/site/jacoco (the HTML report index.html and the XML report jacoco.xml, the parameter
            formats; the folder is in .gitignore through target/). The XML report is the deterministic
            source that the recipe asserts on (the counters of the report element). The configuration has
            no check goal and no rule: the recipe makes a report and no threshold is set (REQ-006). The
            version is the one of tools/versions.env (JACOCO_VERSION, just check-pins compares it). -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.jacoco</groupId>
        <artifactId>jacoco-maven-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${jacoco.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <formats>
            <format>XML</format>
            <format>HTML</format>
          </formats>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.openapitools</groupId>
        <artifactId>openapi-generator-maven-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${openapi-generator.version}</version>
        <executions>
          <!-- The Spring server interfaces (REQ-004). Options: the four of the task 090.120 (interfaceOnly,
               skipDefaultInterface, hideGenerationTimestamp and generateSupportingFiles), and the options that the
               agent set (see the plan, Decisions Made). -->
          <execution>
            <id>spring-interfaces</id>
            <phase>generate-sources</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>generate</goal>
            </goals>
            <configuration>
              <inputSpec>${contract.file}</inputSpec>
              <generatorName>spring</generatorName>
              <output>${generated.java.dir}</output>
              <apiPackage>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.api</apiPackage>
              <modelPackage>biz.dfch.specmgrdemo.model</modelPackage>
              <generateSupportingFiles>false</generateSupportingFiles>
              <generateApiTests>false</generateApiTests>
              <generateModelTests>false</generateModelTests>
              <generateApiDocumentation>false</generateApiDocumentation>
              <generateModelDocumentation>false</generateModelDocumentation>
              <addCompileSourceRoot>true</addCompileSourceRoot>
              <configOptions>
                <interfaceOnly>true</interfaceOnly>
                <skipDefaultInterface>true</skipDefaultInterface>
                <hideGenerationTimestamp>true</hideGenerationTimestamp>
                <useSpringBoot4>true</useSpringBoot4>
                <sourceFolder>java</sourceFolder>
                <annotationLibrary>none</annotationLibrary>
                <documentationProvider>none</documentationProvider>
                <openApiNullable>false</openApiNullable>
                <!-- Both are the defaults of 7.27.0. The generator writes a warning if they are not set. -->
                <generateJsonIncludeAnnotations>false</generateJsonIncludeAnnotations>
                <generateJsonSetterNullsAnnotations>false</generateJsonSetterNullsAnnotations>
              </configOptions>
            </configuration>
          </execution>
          <!-- The API documentation (REQ-015): the generator html2. No phase: `just api-docs` starts it with
               the goal openapi-generator:generate@api-docs. The output is not in git. -->
          <execution>
            <id>api-docs</id>
            <phase>none</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>generate</goal>
            </goals>
            <configuration>
              <inputSpec>${contract.file}</inputSpec>
              <generatorName>html2</generatorName>
              <output>${api-docs.dir}</output>
              <addCompileSourceRoot>false</addCompileSourceRoot>
              <configOptions>
                <hideGenerationTimestamp>true</hideGenerationTimestamp>
              </configOptions>
            </configuration>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
